        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "59807a0e-1d23-5183-b5ca-db6af452db4c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Inter-Allied Socialist Conferences of World War I, First World War, 1900 Hoboken Docks Fire\n- Organizations: socialist parties of the Entente or Allied powers\n- Countries/Blocs: Allies of World War I, Entente Powers, Central Powers\n- Products: SS Main (1900)\n- Places: Bremen, Baltimore\n\nFacts:\n- During the First World War, the Allies of World War I, also called the Entente Powers, were the countries that opposed the Central Powers.\n- During the First World War, there were several Inter-Allied Socialist Conferences involving the socialist parties of the Entente or Allied powers.\n- SS Main was launched in 1900 and served on the route from Bremen to Baltimore.\n- SS Main was involved in the 1900 Hoboken Docks Fire.\n- In 1914, the Allies of World War I seized SS Main, ending her service that had continued from her 1900 launch.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
